IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `fwr-common`

-- Fair Work Regulations 2009 (Cth) -- baseline-2026-11: deductions from pay (regs 2.12A, 2.12) and pay slips (regs 3.45
-- to 3.48).
--
-- Seat: the employee checking whether a deduction from their pay was allowed and whether their pay slips say what they
-- must, typically while working out an underpayment claim (ss 324, 326 and 536 of the Act are civil remedy provisions
-- the employee can sue on).
--
-- Edition: Compilation No. 57 (F2026C00996), as deposited at ../../registers/source-bundle/F2009L02356.txt.

§ `reg 2.12A -- what a written authorisation of a deduction must say`

-- Reg 2.12A(1), for a deduction of a specified amount (s 324(2)(a)(i) of the Act): the authorisation "must also include
-- ... (a) the purpose of the deduction; (b) the date on which the deduction is to be made; (c) the name of the person to
-- whom the amount of the deduction is to be given."
-- (2), for "multiple or ongoing deductions" (s 324(2)(a)(ii)): "(a) the purpose of the deductions; (b) if the
-- deductions are for a specified amount or amounts--those amounts; (c) either: (i) the dates on which the deductions are
-- to be made; or (ii) the date after which, and the frequency with which, the deductions are to be made; (d) the name of
-- the person to whom the amounts of the deductions are to be given."
-- (3): "This regulation does not apply in relation to an authorisation covered by clause 90 of Schedule 1 to the Act"
-- (one saved from before the 2023 amendments): NOTHING, as the regulation says nothing about it.
@export Does my written authorisation for a deduction from my pay include what the regulations require (reg 2.12A)?
GIVEN `it was given before the 2023 changes and saved by clause 90` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether your authorisation is one made before the 2023 amendments and kept in force by clause 90 of Schedule 1 to the Act
      `it is for multiple or ongoing deductions` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the authorisation is for more than one deduction or ongoing deductions (rather than a single deduction of a specified amount)
      `it states the purpose` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether it states the purpose of the deduction or deductions
      `it states the date or dates` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether it states the date of the deduction, or the dates of the deductions, or the date after which and how often they are to be made
      `it names who gets the money` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether it names the person to whom the amount deducted is to be given
      `the deductions are of specified amounts` IS A BOOLEAN @desc For multiple or ongoing deductions: whether they are for a specified amount or amounts
      `it states those amounts` IS A BOOLEAN @desc For multiple or ongoing deductions of specified amounts: whether it states those amounts
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Does my deduction authorisation include what is required` IS
    IF `it was given before the 2023 changes and saved by clause 90`
    THEN NOTHING
    ELSE JUST (    `it states the purpose`
               AND `it states the date or dates`
               AND `it names who gets the money`
               AND (    (NOT `it is for multiple or ongoing deductions`)
                     OR (NOT `the deductions are of specified amounts`)
                     OR `it states those amounts`))

§ `reg 2.12 -- reasonable and unreasonable deductions`

-- Reg 2.12(1): "a circumstance in which a deduction ... is reasonable is that: (a) the deduction is made in respect of
-- the provision of goods or services: (i) by an employer, or a party related to the employer; and (ii) to an employee;
-- and (b) the goods or services are provided in the ordinary course of the business of the employer or related party;
-- and (c) the goods or services are provided to members of the general public on: (i) the same terms and conditions ...;
-- or (ii) ... terms and conditions that are not more favourable to the members of the general public."
-- (2): reasonable if "the deduction is for the purpose of recovering costs directly incurred by the employer as a
-- result of the voluntary private use of particular property of the employer by an employee (whether authorised or not)."
-- (3): "subject to subregulations (1) and (2), a circumstance in which a deduction ... is not reasonable is that the
-- deduction is for an amount that may be varied from time to time."
-- These are circumstances, not a closed list: where none holds the regulations do not answer (NOTHING), and s 326(1)
-- of the Act is left to decide the deduction on its own terms.
@export Do the regulations say a deduction from my pay that benefits my employer is reasonable (reg 2.12)?
GIVEN `it pays for goods or services my employer or a related party gave me` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the deduction pays for goods or services provided to you by your employer or a party related to your employer
      `they sell those goods or services in the ordinary course of business` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether those goods or services are provided in the ordinary course of that business
      `the public gets them on terms no better than mine` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether members of the public get those goods or services on the same terms as you, or on terms no more favourable than yours
      `it recovers costs of my voluntary private use of my employer's property` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the deduction recovers costs your employer directly incurred because of your voluntary private use of its property (for example personal calls on a work phone)
      `the amount can be varied from time to time` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the deduction is for an amount that may be varied from time to time
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is the deduction reasonable under the regulations` IS
    IF    (    `it pays for goods or services my employer or a related party gave me`
           AND `they sell those goods or services in the ordinary course of business`
           AND `the public gets them on terms no better than mine`)
       OR `it recovers costs of my voluntary private use of my employer's property`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE IF `the amount can be varied from time to time`
         THEN JUST FALSE
         ELSE NOTHING

§ `regs 3.45, 3.46 -- what a pay slip must show`

-- Reg 3.45: "a pay slip must be: (a) in electronic form; or (b) a hard copy."
-- Reg 3.46(1): "a pay slip must specify: (a) the employer's name; and (b) the employee's name; and (c) the period to
-- which the pay slip relates; and (d) the date on which the payment ... was made; and (e) the gross amount of the
-- payment; and (f) the net amount of the payment; and (g) any amount paid to the employee that is a bonus, loading,
-- allowance, penalty rate, incentive-based payment or other separately identifiable entitlement; and (h) on and after 1
-- January 2010--the Australian Business Number (if any) of the employer."
@export Does my pay slip show the basic details it must (regs 3.45, 3.46(1))?
GIVEN `it is electronic or on paper` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the pay slip is in electronic form or a hard copy
      `it shows my employer's name and mine` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether it shows both your employer's name and your name
      `it shows the pay period and the payment date` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether it shows the period it covers and the date the payment was made
      `it shows the gross and net amounts` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether it shows both the gross and the net amount of the payment
      `it shows each bonus, loading, allowance, penalty rate or incentive paid` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether it shows every bonus, loading, allowance, penalty rate, incentive payment or other separately identifiable entitlement paid (true if none was paid)
      `it shows my employer's ABN, or my employer has none` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether it shows your employer's Australian Business Number, or your employer has no ABN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Does my pay slip show the basic details` IF
        `it is electronic or on paper`
    AND `it shows my employer's name and mine`
    AND `it shows the pay period and the payment date`
    AND `it shows the gross and net amounts`
    AND `it shows each bonus, loading, allowance, penalty rate or incentive paid`
    AND `it shows my employer's ABN, or my employer has none`

-- Reg 3.46(2): "If one or more amounts are deducted ... under subsection 324(1) of the Act, the pay slip must also
-- include, for each deduction: (a) the amount of the deduction; and (b) the name, or the name and number, of the fund or
-- account into which the deduction was paid."
-- (3): "If the employee is paid at an hourly rate of pay, the pay slip must also include: (a) the rate of pay for the
-- employee's ordinary hours ...; and (b) the number of hours in that period for which the employee was employed at that
-- rate; and (c) the amount of the payment made at that rate."
-- (4): "If the employee is paid at an annual rate of pay, the pay slip must also include the rate as at the latest date
-- to which the payment relates."
@export Does my pay slip show my deductions and my rate of pay as it must (reg 3.46(2)-(4))?
GIVEN `amounts were deducted from my pay` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether any amount was deducted from this payment
      `it shows each deduction and the fund or account it went to` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether it shows the amount of each deduction and the name (or name and number) of the fund or account it was paid into
      `I am paid by the hour` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you are paid at an hourly rate
      `it shows my ordinary hourly rate, the hours and the amount at that rate` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether it shows your ordinary hourly rate, the hours worked at that rate in the period, and the amount paid at that rate
      `I am paid at an annual rate` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you are paid at an annual rate (a salary)
      `it shows my annual rate at the end of the period` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether it shows your annual rate as at the latest date the payment relates to
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Does my pay slip show my deductions and rate` IF
        ((NOT `amounts were deducted from my pay`) OR `it shows each deduction and the fund or account it went to`)
    AND ((NOT `I am paid by the hour`) OR `it shows my ordinary hourly rate, the hours and the amount at that rate`)
    AND ((NOT `I am paid at an annual rate`) OR `it shows my annual rate at the end of the period`)

-- Reg 3.46(5): if the employer "has made, or intends to make, superannuation contributions", the pay slip must include
-- "(a) the amount of each contribution that the employer made during the period ..., and the name, or the name and
-- number, of any fund to which the contribution was made; or (b) the amounts of contributions that the employer intends
-- to make in relation to the period ..., and the name, or the name and number, of any fund".
-- (5A): the fund's name need not be shown if "(a) the pay slip is required to be given to the employee within the period
-- of 14 days commencing on the first day on which the employer pays an amount to the employee ...; and (b) by the time
-- the pay slip is given ...: (i) there is no chosen fund for the employee ...; and (ii) the Commissioner of Taxation has
-- not notified the employer ... of whether the Commissioner is satisfied that there is a stapled fund".
-- (6): contributions to a defined benefit interest are not "contributions" here.
@export Does my pay slip show my superannuation contributions as it must (reg 3.46(5)-(6))?
GIVEN `my employer makes or will make accumulation super contributions for me` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether your employer has made, or intends to make, superannuation contributions for you (other than to a defined benefit interest)
      `it shows the contribution amounts` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether it shows the amount of each contribution made in the period, or the amounts intended for the period
      `it shows the fund's name` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether it shows the name (or name and number) of the fund
      `the slip was due within 14 days of my first pay` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether this pay slip had to be given within the 14 days starting on the day you were first paid
      `I had no chosen fund when it was given` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether, when it was given, you had no chosen super fund
      `the ATO had not yet told my employer about a stapled fund` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether, when it was given, the Commissioner of Taxation had not yet told your employer whether there is a stapled fund for you
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Does my pay slip show my super` IF
        (NOT `my employer makes or will make accumulation super contributions for me`)
    OR (    `it shows the contribution amounts`
        AND (   `it shows the fund's name`
             OR (    `the slip was due within 14 days of my first pay`
                 AND `I had no chosen fund when it was given`
                 AND `the ATO had not yet told my employer about a stapled fund`)))

§ `regs 3.47, 3.48 -- family and domestic violence leave on a pay slip`

-- Reg 3.47: the information that "must not be included in a pay slip is: (a) a statement that an amount paid ... is a
-- payment in respect of the employee's entitlement to paid family and domestic violence leave; and (b) a statement that a
-- period of leave ... has been taken as ... paid family and domestic violence leave; and (c) the balance of an
-- employee's entitlement to paid family and domestic violence leave."
-- Reg 3.48(2): an amount paid for such leave "(a) must not be reported on a pay slip as an amount paid ... for taking a
-- period of leave; and (b) must instead be reported ... (i) for the performance of the employee's ordinary hours of
-- work; or (ii) as another kind of payment made in relation to the performance of the employee's work"; (3) unless the
-- employee asked for it to be reported as "a particular kind of leave (other than ... paid family and domestic violence
-- leave)".
-- The answer is whether the pay slip broke these rules (TRUE means it did). The 4-month grace period of reg 7.06 is out
-- of scope (NOTES.md).
@export Does my pay slip wrongly show my family and domestic violence leave (regs 3.47, 3.48)?
GIVEN `it says a payment or a period was family and domestic violence leave` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the pay slip says any payment or any period of leave was paid family and domestic violence leave
      `it shows my family and domestic violence leave balance` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether it shows the balance of your paid family and domestic violence leave
      `it reports my family and domestic violence leave pay as leave` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether it reports the pay for your family and domestic violence leave as pay for leave of any kind (rather than as ordinary hours or another work payment)
      `I asked for it to be shown as another kind of leave` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you asked your employer to report that pay as a particular other kind of leave
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Does my pay slip wrongly show family and domestic violence leave` IF
        `it says a payment or a period was family and domestic violence leave`
    OR `it shows my family and domestic violence leave balance`
    OR (`it reports my family and domestic violence leave pay as leave` AND (NOT `I asked for it to be shown as another kind of leave`))
